  "text_sample": "Your Page Title Styrke 00 Classes left today Overview Free trial Menu \u203a Timetable \u203a Classes \u203a Coaches \u203a Memberships \u203a Personal training \u203a Journal \u203a Overview \u203a About \u203a FAQ \u203a Contact \u203a Free trial Today Open now Hours Mon\u2013Fri 06\u201322 Sat\u2013Sun 08\u201318 Find us N\u00f8rrebrogade 88 2200 Copenhagen N Desk +45 33 12 88 00 [email protected] Follow Instagram Strava Spotify Start a free week Journal Mobility Why your hips feel tight, and what actually helps Tight hips are rarely short muscles. They are usually hips that have forgotten a position. Three drills that remind them. Giulia Conti Mobility and pilates 21 Aug 2026 , 1 min read \u201cMy hips are tight\u201d is the sentence I hear most at the desk. Usually it comes from someone who sits all day and squats three times a week. Here is the surprise: in most people the muscles are not short. The nervous system simply does not trust the end of the range, so it stops you before you get there. Stretching harder does not fix that. Using the range, slowly and often, does. 1. The 90/90 switch Sit with both knees bent at ninety degrees, one in front, one to the side. Rotate slowly to the other side without using your hands. Ten slow switches. 2. The supported squat H",
